 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Chosen over five-second HTTPS polling and hosted realtime services. Accepts connection management and reconnect complexity to achieve subsecond updates without recurring fees or provider coupling. The change store provides replayable revisions; delivery manages WebSocket sessions; browser sync handles subscription, reconnect, and catch-up.
